# The root task boots (M5): boot steps 6 to 9 build its CNode, VSpace,
# image frames and TCB from the root ELF in .rootimage, which is then
# unmapped and reclaimed; step 10 hands the TCB to the scheduler, which
# enters it by iretq. `test=root` is no kernel self-test, so the root task
# runs it. The stub prints its lines through DebugPutChar, one sysretq per
# byte, and ends the run with DebugHalt(0).
cmdline: test=root
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=root"
expect: boot: root task: image 0x400000-
expect: , entry 0x400000; TCB at
expect: boot: .rootimage
expect: unmapped from the kernel window and reclaimed as RAM untyped
expect: test=root: not a kernel self-test; the root task runs it
expect: boot: entering the root task at 0x400000 in ring 3
expect: root: microL4 root task, BootInfo at
expect: root: image 0x400000-
expect: root: cmdline "test=root"
expect: root: paging structures: slots 17-19, 3
expect: root: image frames: slots 20-
expect: root: extra BootInfo frames: slots 16-16, 1
expect: root: untyped: slots
expect: root: empty: slots
expect: untyped,
expect: KiB of RAM; TSC
# DebugDumpScheduler: the root TCB, current, at priority 255.
expect: : Running, priority 255, at 0x4
expect:  *
expect: root: back from Yield, the only thread at its priority
# Untyped_Retype with MR4, MR5 and the destination CNode's CPtr in the IPC
# buffer. Its first retype clears the whole untyped, which the timer
# preempts again and again: each time the thread restarts its syscall.
expect: root: Untyped_Retype of the
expect: MiB untyped in slot
expect: into a 4 KiB frame in slot
expect: : done
expect: root: a Call on empty slot
expect: : InvalidCapability, MR0 0
expect: TEST PASS
expect: dispatch: invocations preempted and restarted:
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
